truct-ops holds at most 64 members."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::BPF_BASE_TYPE_BITS","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_type_flag","include/linux/bpf.h::DYNPTR_TYPE_FLAG_MASK","include/linux/bpf.h::BPF_BASE_TYPE_LIMIT","include/linux/bpf.h::BPF_TYPE_LIMIT","include/linux/bpf.h::MAX_BPF_FUNC_ARGS","include/linux/bpf.h::MAX_BPF_FUNC_REG_ARGS","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_access_type","include/linux/bpf.h::BTF_FMODEL_SIGNED_ARG","include/linux/bpf.h::BTF_FMODEL_ARENA_ARG","include/linux/bpf.h::BTF_FMODEL_NULLABLE_ARG","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_reg_type"],"text":"Low 8 bits hold base types with derived limits; high bits are modifiers. Arity 12/5 regs; access 1 read 2 write. Fmodel and reg vocabularies mark signed/arena/nullable roles."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map.anon_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_obj_memcpy","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_obj_memzero","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_obj_swap_uptrs","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_flags_to_cap","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_flags_access_ok","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_owner_alloc","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_owner_free","include/linux/bpf.h::map_type_contains_progs"],"text":"Freeze/cookie are write-once; reclamation union holds one role. Copies preserve specials. Flags map to read/write caps. Owners zero-alloced. Prog maps are prog array, devmap, cpumap."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::is_tracing_multi","include/linux/bpf.h::is_struct_ops_tramp","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_fsession_cnt","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_calls_session_cookie","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_fsession_cookie_cnt","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_trampoline_link_cgroup_shim","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_trampoline_unlink_cgroup_shim","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_rcu_lock_held","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_allow_ptr_leaks","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_token_capable","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_allow_uninit_stack","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_bypass_spec_v1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_bypass_spec_v4","include/linux/kernel.h::might_fault.alt_1","include/linux/kernel.h::might_fault.alt_2"],"text":"Multi is fentry/fexit/fsession-multi; struct-ops needs one node. Sessions scan fentry. Cgroup shim unsupported. RCU held if any hold. Leak/spec need perfmon or no mitigations; might-fault debug-only."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::register_bpf_struct_ops.alt_1","include/linux/bpf.h::register_bpf_struct_ops.alt_2","include/linux/bpf.h::BPF_MODULE_OWNER","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dummy_ops_state","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dummy_ops","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_try_module_get.alt_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_module_put.alt_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_try_module_get.alt_2","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_module_put.alt_2","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_supported","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_map_sys_lookup_elem","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_link_create","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_assoc_struct_ops","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_disassoc_struct_ops","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_get_assoc_struct_ops","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_struct_ops_info_fill","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_desc_release"],"text":"Enabled registration wraps payload; disabled returns zero. Sentinel selects struct-ops vs generic refs; disabled reports unsupported with no-op release. Dummy offers test calls."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_get_recursion_context","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_put_recursion_context","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dynptr_kern","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dynptr_check_off_len"],"text":"Recursion allows one entry per CPU context with paired acquire/release. Dynptr packs len/type/readonly; usable len must be masked and offset+len checked."},{"sids":["include/linux/list.h::INIT_LIST_HEAD","include/linux/math.h::round_up","include/linux/minmax.h::swap","include/linux/rbtree.h::RB_CLEAR_NODE","include/linux/refcount.h::refcount_set","include/linux/percpu-defs.h::this_cpu_dec","include/linux/sched.h::migrate_disable","include/linux/sched.h::migrate_enable","include/asm-generic/rwonce.h: