:1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F2"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F4"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p10","crown":"A","phase":"F5"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p13","crown":"A","phase":"F6"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_state"],"text":"Maps go init/active with refs, optional permanent freeze, then deferred free via callback or work. Struct-ops moves INIT/READY/INUSE/TOBEFREE."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_tramp_skip","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_tramp_image","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_trampoline","include/linux/bpf.h::__BPF_DISPATCHER_SC_INIT.alt_1","include/linux/bpf.h::__BPF_DISPATCHER_SC_INIT.alt_2","include/linux/bpf.h::BPF_DISPATCHER_INIT","include/linux/bpf.h::__BPF_DISPATCHER_CALL.alt_1","include/linux/bpf.h::__BPF_DISPATCHER_CALL.alt_2"],"text":"Tramp images publish as current while old images linger until last use, with temp slot for multi-attach. Dispatchers init empty; calls route via static slot or direct by build."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_offload"],"text":"Offload records track attach state and optimization failure with generated images from preparation through teardown."}],"structs":[{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map.anon_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_owner","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_array","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_array.anon_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_event_entry"],"text":"Maps hold identity, dims, flags, BTF/memcg with freeze mutex, atomics, work/callback union, owner lock and once-fields. Arrays add size/mask/aux; events link files with RCU."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_map_dev_ops","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_offloaded_map","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dynptr_kern","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dynptr_type","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_stream_id","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_stream_elem","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_stream","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_stream_stage.alt_1"],"text":"Offloaded maps embed generic map plus netdev/ops/private. Dynptr packs addr/len/off with type/readonly. Streams chain elems with stack, mutexed backlog and staging."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_func_proto","include/linux/bpf.h::btf_func_model","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_insn_access_aux","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_ctx_arg_aux","include/linux/bpf.h::btf_mod_pair"],"text":"Prototypes fix 5-reg convention, flags, classes and authorization. Func models store widths/attrs. Aux records carry widths, type refs and logs; mod pairs bind types to modules."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_tramp_skip","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_tramp_image","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_trampoline","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_attach_target_info","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dispatcher","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_dispatcher_prog","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_ksym","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_tramp_prog_type","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_func_info_aux","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_jit_poke_descriptor","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_jit_poke_reason","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_sig_verdict","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_sig_keyring"],"text":"Tramps use skips/images with per-kind tables and current/history images. Dispatchers hold fixed tables. Ksym, attach, poke, aux and signatures track symbols and updates."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_stream_id"],"text":"Progs hold type/attach/len/jited/tag/stats/guards/func/aux with JIT/license/blind/sleep flags. Array aux tracks pokes. Links hold ref/id/type/ops/prog/flags with RCU/work union and ops for release/dealloc/detach/update/info/poll. Tramp nodes, mounts and tokens complete attach."},{"sids":["include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_aux","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_array_item","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_array_item.anon_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_prog_array","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_run_ctx","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_cg_run_ctx","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_trace_run_ctx","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_tramp_run_ctx","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_arg_info","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_desc","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_struct_ops_common_value","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_iter_task_type","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_iter_aux_info","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_iter_aux_info.anon_1","include/linux/bpf.h::bpf_iter_aux_info.anon_2"],"text":"Prog aux groups identity, limits, attach, flags, JIT, maps and debug. Arrays chain items with cookie union. Run contexts extend base for cgroup/trace/tramp. Struct-ops and iter aux describe ops and walks."}],"stubs":[]}
